HST Office: Ctrl+Shift+A toggles All Caps in HST Writer, as in the reference suite (owner decision 2026-11-15).

- .uno:HstAllCaps (FN_HST_SET_ALL_CAPS): the character attribute "All caps" (SvxCaseMap::Uppercase), toggled like Small
  Caps (.uno:SmallCaps) in SwTextShell::ExecCharAttr: on when the selection is not all caps, off when it is. The text
  itself is unchanged, so turning it off gives the typed letters back; Format ▸ Character ▸ Font Effects shows it as
  Case "UPPERCASE". The state follows the selection (GetAttrState).
- Ctrl+Shift+A (macOS Cmd+Shift+A, the Mac edition's key too) runs it; it was Left-To-Right paragraph, which stays on
  the Format menu and the ribbon.
License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).
Test: scripts/check-keytips-parity.py (data/ribbon/shortcuts-office-parity.json), tests/runtime/check-shortcut-parity-runtime.py.
